== Tests (core/tests/unittest and/or contract tests) ==
Add unit/contract tests for BOTH zlink_recv (PAIR and DEALER) and zlink_router_recv (ROUTER):
- multipart record: exact part count, byte-exact part order/content.
- router DATA -> reply_token 0; router REQUEST -> same nonzero token, same source RID on the record.
- capacity too small -> ZLINK_RECV_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL, *part_count_out_ = needed count, record NOT
  consumed; retry with adequate capacity yields the identical record exactly once (part-for-part).
- DONTWAIT with no data -> ZLINK_RECV_NO_DATA/EAGAIN; with a queued record -> whole record.
- ownership: each returned slot closes exactly once (zlink_multipart_close); no leak, no double free.
- record atomicity: whole record or nothing (no half record on DONTWAIT).
- mixing: after a *_recv_part has taken part 1 of a multi-part record, a whole-message recv returns
  EBUSY; and a capacity-miss stage followed by *_recv_part drains the staged record correctly.
- single-part record via whole-message recv (count == 1).
Follow the existing test style. If you move/rename any shared test helper, keep assertions intact.

